WEBVTT

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:42.000
Wow, I'm finally going to see
my favorite chef, TV's Elzar!

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.628
Oh, this is the greatest
nanosecond of my life.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.005
No, this one is. No, this one. Wait...

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:48.632
That one was slightly worse.

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:50.801
Ah, so far so good on this one.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:54.096
And now, here he is.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:57.641
Chef, restaurateur, author
of Cooking Slugs for Dinner

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.352
and Cooking Dinner for Slugs...

00:01:00.853 --> 00:01:03.063
Elzar!

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:06.525
All right! yeah!

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.443
Yeah, baby! Whoo!

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:13.115
Elzar!

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:16.159
All right!

00:01:16.994 --> 00:01:18.704
Elzar, you're my god.

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:21.248
Please sign this sketch
I drew of you.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:27.212
Oh, Elzar, bless you!

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:30.090
Mmm. Mmm...

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:34.094
Now, this is why I prefer
your nonstick robots.

00:01:39.016 --> 00:01:40.017
Oh...

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.229
All right! Yeah!

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:45.439
Whoo!

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:49.484
All right, yeah. Whoo.

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:53.906
- Hey, I hope you folks like Cajun food.
- Hoo-whee!

00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:57.534
'Cause today we're making
Elzar's down-home Neptune-style gumbo.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:00.579
Now, step one.
You want to boil some oysters

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:03.498
in a pot of down-home,
Neptune-style gumbo.

00:02:03.582 --> 00:02:05.709
Boiled? Interesting!

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.128
Bender,
please try to be a little quieter.

00:02:08.212 --> 00:02:09.505
No, youshut up!

00:02:09.588 --> 00:02:12.758
Of course, every now and then,
you want to knock it up a notch

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:15.469
with a blast from your spice weasel. Bam!

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:17.596
Oh, yeah! Bam it again, Elzar!

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:18.847
Knock it up another notch.

00:02:18.931 --> 00:02:21.183
Geez, who let this guy
through the metal detector?

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.352
Come on, you wimp, work that weasel!

00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:24.686
Quit holding out on us!

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.940
If you promise
to stop interrupting, all right.

00:02:28.023 --> 00:02:30.984
Against my will, I'm going
to knock it up another notch.

00:02:31.527 --> 00:02:33.779
I got to get this
notch up knocking on film.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:35.322
Hey, Elzar, think fast!

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:36.406
Wha... Huh?

00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:38.242
My eye!

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:39.660
I'm blind!

00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:42.788
Bam!

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:52.506
Tell me, Doctor, how's my cyst?

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.007
Grande.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:02:59.263
I don't like the looks of this doctor.

00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:02.099
I bet I've lost
more patients than he's even treated.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.601
Okay, what does this look like to you?

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:05.727
Um...

00:03:05.811 --> 00:03:06.979
A grayish blob?

00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:08.814
Right. And this one?

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:09.898
Um...

00:03:09.982 --> 00:03:11.066
A grayish blob?

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:13.318
Not as right that time.

00:03:13.402 --> 00:03:16.488
It looks like you might have
some mild corneal irritation.

00:03:16.572 --> 00:03:18.407
Nice try, little boy.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.452
You may have your textbook knowledge
and your real diploma,

00:03:22.536 --> 00:03:26.748
but I have more skill in my little claw
than you have in your whole carapace.

00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:30.836
You seem a bit tense. Here, try these.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:33.255
Sure, butter me up with candy.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.965
Well, it won't work, sonny.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.596
Why always the fighting?

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:42.181
Your eye just needs some rest.

00:03:42.264 --> 00:03:44.349
You'll have to wear this patch
for about a week.

00:03:44.474 --> 00:03:46.018
Oh! A week?

00:03:46.101 --> 00:03:47.895
What do youthink, Dr. Zoidberg?

00:03:48.854 --> 00:03:49.855
Clack.

00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:56.320
Thanks for the help, Leela.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:01.200
Leela, we're right here!

00:04:01.283 --> 00:04:04.870
I'm not deaf. I just have
to wear this stupid eye patch.

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:06.747
- Does it look stupid?
- No.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.709
In fact, it looks so nice
I think I might get one, too.

00:04:11.627 --> 00:04:12.753
It's Elzar again!

00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:16.423
Oh, my God, I'm so excited,
I wish I could wet my pants!

00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:19.259
Leela, please, let me make this up to you.

00:04:19.343 --> 00:04:22.679
You and your friends are all invited
to my restaurant tonight.

00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:25.641
I'm going to bam you up
a dinner you'll never forget.

00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:26.767
- All right!
- Oh, yeah!

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.769
- Great!
- Hooray for blindy!

00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:31.730
Oh, God. I'm coming down!

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.402
Folks, tell the neighbors
to watch your mouth

00:04:37.486 --> 00:04:39.780
'cause your taste buds
are going on vacation.

00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:42.032
I made you each your own special meal.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.283
So dig in!

00:04:44.743 --> 00:04:47.704
It's the biggest Jamaican platter
I've ever seen!

00:04:47.788 --> 00:04:50.582
Jerk chicken, jerk beef, jerk pork.

00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:52.835
Is there any meat this man can't jerk?

00:04:52.918 --> 00:04:55.462
The king crab is to die for.

00:04:55.546 --> 00:04:58.048
Look, a tiny edible crown.

00:04:58.549 --> 00:04:59.550
What's it made of?

00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:00.968
Wood.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.636
Mmm! Oh!

00:05:02.886 --> 00:05:05.639
Fry, you got to try the sterno niçoise.

00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:07.266
No, thanks. That's robot food.

00:05:07.349 --> 00:05:08.851
It's so good.

00:05:08.976 --> 00:05:10.394
Oh, just try a little.

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:11.603
No, really, I don't...

00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:12.729
Ahhh!

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:16.733
Mmm!

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:18.527
You doing all right over there, Leela?

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.280
Oh, yeah. This salad's fantastic.

00:05:21.363 --> 00:05:22.531
So fresh.

00:05:27.411 --> 00:05:28.412
Ah!

00:05:34.793 --> 00:05:39.214
Oh, my. That steamed carrot
was a bit spicy for me.

00:05:39.298 --> 00:05:41.049
Everybody enjoy their dinner?

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:44.261
God, yes, Elzar!

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.346
Well, I sure enjoyed cooking for you,

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:49.266
and to make everything completely square,

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:53.187
I want you to have these
complimentary after-dinner chocolates.

00:05:54.813 --> 00:05:56.398
What's this under the chocolates?

00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:58.567
Yeah, you take care of that
whenever you want.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.943
- Hey!
- What?

00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:01.028
A bill?

00:06:01.111 --> 00:06:04.156
You're charging us after you blinded me?

00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:06.867
Hey, I made you a nice meal.
This ain't a charity.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.410
$1,200?

00:06:08.493 --> 00:06:10.454
Holy zombie Jesus!

00:06:10.537 --> 00:06:13.582
We don't have that kind of money,
especially not Zoidberg.

00:06:13.665 --> 00:06:16.084
They took away my credit cards.

00:06:16.168 --> 00:06:17.544
Okay, okay, wait.

00:06:17.628 --> 00:06:19.922
I know how to take care of this,
no problem.

00:06:20.005 --> 00:06:22.966
You deadbeats are under arrest.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.094
It's a stone-cold shame.

00:06:26.637 --> 00:06:28.347
He's making a break for it! Get him!

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.390
No, I was just picking my nose.

00:06:30.474 --> 00:06:31.975
He's picking his nose! Get him!

00:06:39.316 --> 00:06:40.901
The old dine-and-dash, eh?

00:06:40.984 --> 00:06:43.403
My daddy owned a restaurant,
and it's punks like you

00:06:43.487 --> 00:06:44.947
that kept him from going regional.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:46.740
That's why I became a cop.

00:06:46.823 --> 00:06:50.077
Now it's payback time. Aw, yeah.

00:06:50.452 --> 00:06:52.746
Please don't hit me. I'm brittle!

00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:55.707
Hey, wait a second.
I've got the perfect solution.

00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:57.626
Listen to the smart robot.

00:06:57.709 --> 00:07:00.838
I love cooking, and Elzar's ass
loves getting kissed, right?

00:07:00.921 --> 00:07:01.922
No question.

00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:05.592
So, how about I work part-time
at the restaurant to pay off our debt?

00:07:05.676 --> 00:07:07.010
I don't know.

00:07:07.094 --> 00:07:10.430
I usually hire people
who are a little less unbearable.

00:07:10.556 --> 00:07:12.516
Ooh! Bender's a model employee.

00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:13.767
He's so polite.

00:07:13.851 --> 00:07:16.103
- And hardworking.
- He's made of candy.

00:07:16.186 --> 00:07:18.689
Okay, fine, I'll give it a shot.

00:07:20.566 --> 00:07:21.608
Hot diggity!

00:07:21.692 --> 00:07:24.111
You better keep your nose clean.

00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:26.905
That'll be easy.
I never wear the damn thing.

00:07:31.493 --> 00:07:34.872
Ah! Time for my precious
10:00 a.m. meeting.

00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:37.708
Where in Legoland is Leela?

00:07:37.791 --> 00:07:38.834
I'm here,

00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:41.378
and I'm getting along just fine,
thank you.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:44.590
My walk to work just took
a little longer today than usual.

00:07:44.673 --> 00:07:46.842
Nibbler took me through the zoo
for some reason.

00:07:51.972 --> 00:07:54.975
Leela, a little help
is nothing to be embarrassed about.

00:07:55.058 --> 00:07:56.602
Like, maybe I could do your makeup.

00:07:56.685 --> 00:07:58.145
I don't need help.

00:07:58.228 --> 00:08:01.231
For your information,
I did this all by myself.

00:08:01.315 --> 00:08:03.150
You look beautiful!

00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:06.028
Incidentally,
my favorite artist is Picasso.

00:08:06.111 --> 00:08:08.197
Well, I'm off to work at the restaurant.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.574
One of you will have to
fill in for me while I'm gone.

00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:14.536
Better yet,
I'll build someone to fill in for you.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.831
Some kind of gamma-powered
mechanical monster

00:08:17.915 --> 00:08:22.669
with freeway on-ramps for arms
and a heart as black as coal.

00:08:22.753 --> 00:08:25.672
Well, if that new guy can't handle things,
give me a call.

00:08:27.216 --> 00:08:29.510
I'm done siphoning out the grease trap.

00:08:29.593 --> 00:08:31.762
I think I need a mint.

00:08:31.929 --> 00:08:34.139
So, what job do I move up to?

00:08:34.223 --> 00:08:37.309
Pastry chef? Saucier? Soup guy?

00:08:37.392 --> 00:08:38.477
Bam!

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.979
Bam yourself.

00:08:45.526 --> 00:08:46.693
Hey, who are they?

00:08:46.777 --> 00:08:49.279
Let's just say they're very good customers

00:08:49.363 --> 00:08:51.532
and I'm not answering any more questions.

00:08:51.615 --> 00:08:53.909
- Are they the robot mafia?
- Yes.

00:08:53.992 --> 00:08:55.494
You call this a table?

00:08:55.911 --> 00:08:57.621
You call this a table?

00:08:57.704 --> 00:08:59.998
I wouldn't hit a guy
over the head with this table.

00:09:00.082 --> 00:09:02.042
You hear that? The Donbot don't like it.

00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:04.378
I ought to clamp you!
You want to be clamped?

00:09:04.545 --> 00:09:06.630
Whoa, whoa. Calm down, Clamps.

00:09:06.713 --> 00:09:10.676
The boss, he likes a wall
against which his back can be put against.

00:09:10.759 --> 00:09:12.177
Such as like this there.

00:09:12.261 --> 00:09:13.637
But that table's already...

00:09:13.762 --> 00:09:15.722
Ah... Let me bus that for you gentlemen.

00:09:18.141 --> 00:09:19.852
No. What I meant to do was...

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.313
I can't believe this!

00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:25.482
Mind your own business and get out!

00:09:28.652 --> 00:09:29.653
Huh.

00:09:29.736 --> 00:09:31.905
I like this guy's lack of style.

00:09:33.156 --> 00:09:36.285
So's I finally give this guy
a pair of cement shoes,

00:09:36.368 --> 00:09:38.912
which he likes
'cause they're lighter than his lead ones.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.416
Hey, you think this computes over here?

00:09:42.499 --> 00:09:44.251
Where's all my change? I gave you a 100.

00:09:44.334 --> 00:09:45.669
No, you gave me a 50.

00:09:45.752 --> 00:09:47.379
- Oh, no, I didn't.
- Yeah, you did.

00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:49.423
Hey, you trying to steal from the Donbot?

00:09:49.506 --> 00:09:51.592
I'm trying, but he's not making it easy.

00:10:01.393 --> 00:10:03.770
Get a load of the ball bearings
on this guy, huh?

00:10:03.854 --> 00:10:06.523
I like you, kid.
Here's something for your trouble.

00:10:06.607 --> 00:10:07.733
It's money.

00:10:07.816 --> 00:10:08.859
Wow, thanks.

00:10:08.942 --> 00:10:10.861
Hey, you earned that 50 bucks.

00:10:10.944 --> 00:10:12.029
You gave me a 20.

00:10:12.112 --> 00:10:14.156
I did? Oh, I'm sorry. I meant...

00:10:14.239 --> 00:10:15.490
Hey, wait a minute.

00:10:18.535 --> 00:10:20.204
I got a good feeling about you.

00:10:20.287 --> 00:10:22.706
Say, you want to work for me
as a hired goon?

00:10:22.789 --> 00:10:25.959
Are you kidding?
I've always wanted to break into gooning.

00:10:26.043 --> 00:10:28.003
Hey, Elzar, I quit!

00:10:28.086 --> 00:10:29.213
'Kay!

00:10:29.796 --> 00:10:32.049
We're going to try you out
with a little delivery job.

00:10:32.132 --> 00:10:35.093
It's for a, uh,
private lottery that we run.

00:10:35.219 --> 00:10:37.304
Wow! You guys run numbers?

00:10:37.387 --> 00:10:40.265
Well, nothing fancy.
You know, ones and zeros mostly.

00:10:40.349 --> 00:10:42.267
Just take this disk over to the pool hall

00:10:42.351 --> 00:10:44.770
and give it to
Sammy "The Mechanical Bull" Gravano.

00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:46.730
And watch out for the cops.

00:10:46.813 --> 00:10:49.024
That's just what my mom used to tell me.

00:10:55.197 --> 00:10:56.198
Whoo!

00:11:05.666 --> 00:11:07.709
That's some fine oil-ade, son.

00:11:07.793 --> 00:11:10.921
We could use a man like you
in the robot mafia,

00:11:11.004 --> 00:11:12.631
which I'm sort of in.

00:11:12.714 --> 00:11:14.716
You flatter me, kind goon,

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:17.177
but I'm only programmed to sell oil-ade

00:11:17.261 --> 00:11:20.055
and write in cute backwards letters
like on the sign here.

00:11:20.931 --> 00:11:22.850
Aw, crap. The cops!

00:11:22.933 --> 00:11:24.518
Seen any suspicious activity?

00:11:24.601 --> 00:11:27.604
Nope, but check out today's Marmaduke.

00:11:27.855 --> 00:11:28.856
Solid.

00:11:28.939 --> 00:11:31.692
Hey, it's that skel from Elzar's.

00:11:31.775 --> 00:11:33.694
Undercover pursuit in progress...

00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:35.320
Baby.

00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:41.618
Gotcha!

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:44.496
What seems to be the problem, officers?
Was I speeding?

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.416
We'll decide what you were doing
after an illegal search.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.545
He's clean.

00:11:51.962 --> 00:11:53.255
Smells nice, too.

00:11:53.338 --> 00:11:55.674
- Better than me?
- Aw, yeah.

00:11:58.927 --> 00:12:00.637
Courtesy of Mr. Bender.

00:12:03.015 --> 00:12:05.559
Nice job, Bender. You passed the test.

00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:08.020
You want to join me,
Clamps and Joey Mousepad

00:12:08.103 --> 00:12:10.814
at our, uh, social club tomorrow night?

00:12:11.064 --> 00:12:13.400
Eh, I'd rather plan some felonies.

00:12:13.567 --> 00:12:16.361
Oh. Then we should meet
at our mafia crime headquarters.

00:12:21.491 --> 00:12:23.243
Donbot, I beg you.

00:12:23.327 --> 00:12:25.454
I can't make this week's loan payment.

00:12:25.537 --> 00:12:30.042
Look into your hard drive
and open your mercy file.

00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:31.960
File not found.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.222
Let that be a warning to you.

00:12:44.097 --> 00:12:45.557
Thank you, Donbot.

00:12:45.933 --> 00:12:48.018
Joey, Clamps, Donnie B.

00:12:48.101 --> 00:12:50.854
Hey, listen, Bender,
we got a big score planned,

00:12:50.938 --> 00:12:52.231
but we need some muscle.

00:12:52.314 --> 00:12:53.607
A little of this, huh?

00:12:53.857 --> 00:12:55.817
Ho, oh, oh. This guy's an ox.

00:12:55.901 --> 00:12:57.611
He's got oxen-like strength.

00:12:57.694 --> 00:12:59.613
Hey, he needs a nickname, right?

00:12:59.696 --> 00:13:00.822
Let's call him "Clamps."

00:13:01.156 --> 00:13:02.157
Clamps?

00:13:02.241 --> 00:13:04.034
That's my name, you numskull!

00:13:04.117 --> 00:13:05.869
Don't make me clamp you one!

00:13:05.953 --> 00:13:07.371
How about "Blotto"?

00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:09.540
It's gritty, it's got street-cred.

00:13:09.623 --> 00:13:11.625
Plus, I can keep my monogrammed slippers.

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:13.293
Good thinking. Hey!

00:13:13.377 --> 00:13:17.381
Now, this score ain't gonna be
no cakewalk in the tea park, all right?

00:13:17.464 --> 00:13:18.882
There may be some death-killing.

00:13:18.966 --> 00:13:22.678
It's going to be clamp this, clamp that,
badda-climp, badda-clamp.

00:13:22.761 --> 00:13:24.263
What do you think, Blotto? You in?

00:13:24.346 --> 00:13:25.514
It's funny.

00:13:25.597 --> 00:13:28.559
Until now,
I always wanted to be a gangster.

00:13:28.934 --> 00:13:30.394
So the answer's yes.

00:13:30.477 --> 00:13:33.438
Hey, hey, way to go,
way to be, way to shoot.

00:13:33.522 --> 00:13:36.733
Now, since we'll be committing crimes
which may be against the law,

00:13:36.817 --> 00:13:38.402
I suggest you have an alibi.

00:13:38.485 --> 00:13:40.237
An alibi, huh?

00:13:44.867 --> 00:13:47.494
I don't feel good.

00:13:47.578 --> 00:13:49.913
I'm genuinely sick.

00:13:49.997 --> 00:13:53.041
But we're about to take off.
We got to eat our blast-off sundaes.

00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:54.459
I can't move.

00:13:54.585 --> 00:13:56.670
Oh, I think I'm going to output.

00:13:56.753 --> 00:13:59.423
Okay, you stay in bed.
I'll eat yours.

00:14:02.551 --> 00:14:03.844
Bender's sick.

00:14:04.845 --> 00:14:07.014
Mmm, need any help taking off?

00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:08.432
I'm fine, thank you.

00:14:08.515 --> 00:14:11.185
A real pilot can navigate by feel alone.

00:14:14.897 --> 00:14:16.857
That's coming out of your pay.

00:14:23.405 --> 00:14:26.200
You know the secret
of traditional robot cooking?

00:14:26.283 --> 00:14:28.869
Start with a good high-quality oil.

00:14:28.952 --> 00:14:30.037
Then eat it.

00:14:30.579 --> 00:14:32.664
So, what's this big score anyway?

00:14:32.748 --> 00:14:35.000
We're heisting a shipment of Zuban cigars.

00:14:35.083 --> 00:14:38.378
Zubans? Those are
the finest cigars in the universe.

00:14:38.462 --> 00:14:41.465
I can stink up a whole maternity ward
with one of those things.

00:14:41.548 --> 00:14:43.217
Yo, there's our pigeon now.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:45.010
Let's shoot bullets out of our guns.

00:15:04.029 --> 00:15:05.822
All right, here's the battle plan.

00:15:05.906 --> 00:15:08.492
We shoot, they surrender, we go aboard,

00:15:08.575 --> 00:15:11.578
somebody does some clamping,
then we heist the cigars and go home.

00:15:11.662 --> 00:15:14.164
And all without killing anyone.

00:15:14.331 --> 00:15:17.751
This gang's got some fresh, new ideas.
I admire that.

00:15:17.876 --> 00:15:19.545
Oh, we'll kill them, all right.

00:15:19.628 --> 00:15:21.380
We got them heavily out-clamped.

00:15:21.463 --> 00:15:22.923
They won't know what clamped them!

00:15:27.469 --> 00:15:29.596
Wow, it's too bad you can't see, Leela,

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.932
'cause there's a cool ship out there
shooting at somebody.

00:15:32.099 --> 00:15:33.684
Whoa!

00:15:33.809 --> 00:15:35.686
I'm taking evasive action.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:39.189
- Uh... Leela?
- Stop bothering me, Fry.

00:15:39.273 --> 00:15:40.774
I need full concentration.

00:16:00.794 --> 00:16:02.296
Missile evaded.

00:16:02.379 --> 00:16:03.755
Eyesight is for chumps.

00:16:03.839 --> 00:16:06.967
Their desire to keep living
shows me no respect.

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:09.678
Hey, Blotto, roll down the window
and start shooting.

00:16:25.485 --> 00:16:27.362
Ooh! He got me!

00:16:27.487 --> 00:16:29.072
What a shot that guy is.

00:16:29.489 --> 00:16:31.491
Wait, why do the raised letters

00:16:31.575 --> 00:16:35.829
that normally say "turn master
steering wheel company" say "Nibbler"?

00:16:35.913 --> 00:16:37.247
Oh, no!

00:16:41.585 --> 00:16:44.213
I'm back at the wheel, Fry.
Everything's under control.

00:16:44.296 --> 00:16:45.839
Great, great.

00:16:45.923 --> 00:16:48.675
The one time I forgot
to buy flight insurance.

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:56.517
They're coming
straight toward our proximity!

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:58.560
Maybe you should give
them the clamps, Clamps.

00:16:58.644 --> 00:16:59.811
Gee, you think?

00:16:59.895 --> 00:17:02.105
You think that maybe
I should use these clamps

00:17:02.189 --> 00:17:05.692
that I use every day at every opportunity?

00:17:05.776 --> 00:17:07.945
You're a freakin' genius, you idiot!

00:17:18.789 --> 00:17:20.040
The engine's stalled.

00:17:20.123 --> 00:17:21.667
I'm trying the manual fuel pump.

00:17:23.794 --> 00:17:24.962
Ahhh!

00:17:25.254 --> 00:17:27.464
Hello, we're the robot mafia.

00:17:27.548 --> 00:17:29.633
The entire robot mafia.

00:17:29.716 --> 00:17:31.385
We're here to steal your cigars.

00:17:31.468 --> 00:17:32.970
You'll never get away with this.

00:17:33.053 --> 00:17:34.304
Unless you let us live.

00:17:34.388 --> 00:17:35.848
Then you'll get off scot-free.

00:17:35.931 --> 00:17:40.060
Joey, Clamps, hurry up and blindfold them
before they see us some more.

00:17:40.978 --> 00:17:44.523
Hey, boss, looks like somebody
beat us to it. Huh?

00:17:44.815 --> 00:17:47.484
I'll assume that's a joke at my expense.

00:17:47.568 --> 00:17:50.195
Well, who's laughing now?

00:17:50.279 --> 00:17:51.947
Hiya!

00:17:53.031 --> 00:17:54.116
Hey, where's Blotto?

00:17:54.199 --> 00:17:56.577
He should be here learning the trade.

00:18:00.497 --> 00:18:02.040
Sorry I'm tardy, old bean.

00:18:02.124 --> 00:18:05.043
I was just enjoying a rather
tasty watercress sandwich.

00:18:05.127 --> 00:18:07.754
Hey, he's more classy than I realized.

00:18:07.838 --> 00:18:08.881
Tie up the prisoners.

00:18:08.964 --> 00:18:10.674
Capital idea, old sport.

00:18:21.894 --> 00:18:24.229
I say, get the hell off me.

00:18:24.313 --> 00:18:26.023
That guy sounds familiar.

00:18:31.528 --> 00:18:33.405
My word, what have we...

00:18:37.743 --> 00:18:39.494
Nothing to see here, old girl.

00:18:39.578 --> 00:18:43.040
Hey, boss, this here crew list
lists a robot on this crew here.

00:18:43.123 --> 00:18:46.502
All right, I want you
to find him and plug him.

00:18:46.585 --> 00:18:48.295
Then unplug him.

00:18:48.378 --> 00:18:49.379
No!

00:18:49.463 --> 00:18:52.216
I got a little surprise in store
for that guy,

00:18:52.299 --> 00:18:53.884
the clamps!

00:18:54.009 --> 00:18:55.427
Huh?

00:18:56.553 --> 00:18:58.972
Wait! Old spice.

00:18:59.806 --> 00:19:01.892
Let me have a go at this mechanized chap.

00:19:01.975 --> 00:19:03.894
I can be quite the rough customer.

00:19:05.938 --> 00:19:07.856
Oh, no, poor Bender.

00:19:07.981 --> 00:19:10.943
I don't feel good.

00:19:12.945 --> 00:19:13.946
Chew on this!

00:19:15.072 --> 00:19:16.114
What-ho!

00:19:17.115 --> 00:19:20.244
Take that, you twit! No, stop it!

00:19:31.046 --> 00:19:32.130
That's the last of them.

00:19:32.214 --> 00:19:34.550
All right, now,
let's mafia things up a bit.

00:19:34.633 --> 00:19:36.176
Joey, burn down the ship.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:37.845
Clamps, burn down the crew.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:41.640
Uh, uh... Donnie, baby,
give me a chance here, huh?

00:19:41.723 --> 00:19:43.141
Youse guys skedaddle.

00:19:43.225 --> 00:19:45.102
Let me take care of the doity woik.

00:19:45.185 --> 00:19:48.772
Hey, I like your attitude
and your latest accent.

00:19:48.856 --> 00:19:52.401
Keep it up and I might just get you
your own pair of clamps, huh?

00:19:54.152 --> 00:19:55.279
The clamps...

00:19:55.362 --> 00:19:57.155
Clamps.

00:19:57.698 --> 00:19:59.741
- Clamps, clamps, clamps.
- Phew!

00:20:03.787 --> 00:20:06.248
Leela, we may not have much time left,

00:20:06.331 --> 00:20:09.293
so let's spend all of it
reminiscing about Bender.

00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:12.421
He was like a big computer
that ran on magic.

00:20:14.923 --> 00:20:16.758
Help! Help!

00:20:16.842 --> 00:20:18.385
- Bender!
- You're okay!

00:20:18.468 --> 00:20:19.553
Yes, I am,

00:20:19.636 --> 00:20:22.181
having just this minute
regained consciousness.

00:20:22.264 --> 00:20:24.266
I've got an idea. Hold still.

00:20:25.809 --> 00:20:26.894
It's about to break.

00:20:26.977 --> 00:20:28.687
Yes! Yes!

00:20:29.146 --> 00:20:32.107
- All right!
- Yeah, it broke, all right!

00:20:34.318 --> 00:20:36.945
I'm telling you,
Leela was cool, she was in command

00:20:37.029 --> 00:20:38.530
and when she kicked people, it hurt.

00:20:38.614 --> 00:20:39.823
It really hurt.

00:20:39.907 --> 00:20:41.742
Well, this is the big moment.

00:20:41.825 --> 00:20:43.994
It's finally time
to take my eye patch off.

00:20:44.077 --> 00:20:45.954
I'll handle the snipping.

00:20:46.038 --> 00:20:48.832
After all, I do have the proper equipment.

00:20:53.545 --> 00:20:55.923
I think it's Blotto.

00:20:56.006 --> 00:20:58.467
That gangster I saw
when my patch fell off.

00:20:58.675 --> 00:21:00.427
Um...

00:21:03.514 --> 00:21:04.681
Professor?

00:21:04.765 --> 00:21:07.100
Where were you at 10:00 p.m. last night?

00:21:07.184 --> 00:21:08.644
Where am I now?

00:21:12.648 --> 00:21:15.192
So they sent a helpless child to kill me.

00:21:15.275 --> 00:21:17.528
Well, I'm not going out without a fight.

00:21:19.279 --> 00:21:22.241
Fine kick, sir, but I'm actually here

00:21:22.324 --> 00:21:24.326
to deliver your cut from the cigar heist.

00:21:24.493 --> 00:21:26.870
Oh, sweet legal tender.

00:21:30.916 --> 00:21:31.917
Ah.

00:21:32.209 --> 00:21:35.629
Kid, tell the Donbot
I'm quitting organized crime.

00:21:35.712 --> 00:21:38.048
From now on,
I'll stick to the regular kind.

00:21:39.508 --> 00:21:40.676
It's funny, Bender.

00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:44.513
With you sick and Leela blind,
only I know what really went on up there.

00:21:44.596 --> 00:21:46.765
Maybe someday
I'll tell you the whole story.

00:21:46.849 --> 00:21:50.477
And maybe someday, I won't listen.